  "definition": "Hydrocephalus is a condition in which too much cerebrospinal fluid builds up inside the skull. It can be linked with enlarged brain ventricles and symptoms such as increased pressure inside the skull, headache, lethargy, urinary incontinence, and problems with coordination.",
